  (text "AUDIO OUT: one 3.5mm jack that drives headphones and also works as a line out\nPer side: AC-coupling cap > 4.7k + 2.2nF low-pass (about 15 kHz, smooths the DAC steps a little)\n> MCP4251 digital pot (volume, set from the encoder over SPI) > NJM4556A buffer (made to drive headphones)\n> 220uF output cap > 33 ohm > jack. The 10k resistors bleed the output cap so plugging in doesn't pop.\nEverything runs from the quiet +5VA rail around a 2.5V mid-point (VREF).\nThe 4.7k load resistors on MOL/MOR are marked 'do not fit'. Try without first; fit them if the chip's\noutput is weak or distorted on the breadboard (milestone M1). Gain is 1x; change it after listening." (at 25.4 22.86 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 38604804-cbd7-5971-a960-47eb7ecd108d)
  )
)
